From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fexiven <48439988+Fexiven@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 13:24:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 23/23] rocket: rk3576: requantise convolutions the way TFLite
 does

Measured on the board, bit for bit on every layer checked, the DPU output
stage of a convolution is

  u   = round_half_even((MAC + A[oc]) * C[oc] / 2^s)          (32 bit)
  out = clamp(round_half_up(u * OUT_CVT_SCALE / 2^OUT_CVT_SHIFT) + offset)

with s from the word RDMA 0x5024 points at and MAC + A equal to TFLite's
int32 accumulator. TFLite rounds acc * M once (M = in_sc * wt_sc / out_sc
in fp32). The encodings used so far, which are also the vendor
runtime's, did not:

 - per tensor: C = 16, s = 4 and a 15 bit OUT_CVT taken from M's mantissa,
   i.e. M quantised to 15 bits;
 - per channel: C = Q14 of wt_sc[oc] / max(wt_sc), so a channel with a
   small scale got a C of a few counts. A dead channel (scale 1e-6) with a
   large bias came out up to 13 off (EfficientDet 012/044/052), MoveNet's
   depthwise layers 2-5 off; the vendor runtime gives the same results
   (bit-identical on MoveNet 020, max 13 on EfficientDet 012);
 - the word 0x1004 also clamps negative values to 0 before the offset,
   which the lift worked around by adding out_zp / M, rounded, to A.

Now C and OUT_CVT are chosen together: per tensor the 15 x 15 bit pair
whose product is closest to M (most fp32 scales factor exactly), per
channel C[oc] over the whole int16 range against the largest M with A[oc]
scaled by the exact C over the rounded one, so the bias comes out right.
s is the smallest shift that keeps u in 32 bits for any input (u wraps
beyond that on the board) and goes into both bytes of the word, as the
vendor's 0x0E0E; there is no lift and the offset takes the zero point.
The regular and the first-conv encoder use it; the int8 per-tensor first
conv takes the A/B/C records instead of the plain bias mode.

Single layers of the 10 test models (1152 conv/depthwise and other ops):
834 bit-exact against the TFLite CPU result instead of 493, 1150 within
one step instead of 1140; the other two (MoveNet depthwise layers with
channel scales below 2^-7 of the largest) are 2 off in under 0.01 % of
the values. Full models: Inception V1 now matches (was max 3),
MobileNetV1 max 4 (was 12), MobileNetV2 max 3 with 2 % of the values off
by more than one (was 6 %), YOLOX max 9 (was 10). The generated small
models: 894 of 894 within one step (was 892).

